  "details": "Hi, so ive been trying to make a fun vr world for my friends, and thought it would be awesome to have a super mario galaxy esc gravity \"walk around a world/ jump onto walls and ceiling\" but then found out how INSAINLY hard it is to assign anything to the base player. for context i was able to get a cube in unity to have the fun gravity, but to do that i need a object or code to go \"hay! that thing works with the gravity\" but, i cant find anything that would allow me to assign the vrc player to the gravity. looked stuff up and all i found said vrc had locked the gravity rotation to down. now i know i could just be dumb. or didnt find the thing. but if this is true and no mater how hard i try im stuck to downwards motion for gravity. i think that is both dumb and stifles creative expression. unless like the only way i could get that gives people the power to like troll in worlds some how. it would be really cool,  if we could have some way to control basic player collisions and rotations.",
